{"title":"Career Roadmap · PLC Programmer","role":"PLC Programmer","summary":"A PLC Programmer develops, programs, tests, commissions and maintains programmable logic controller systems used to automate machines, production lines and industrial processes. The role combines PLC programming, sensors, actuators, electrical systems, HMI/SCADA, industrial networking, motion control and troubleshooting.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build PLC, control, electrical, instrumentation and industrial-networking fundamentals"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Develop expertise in PLC programming, machine automation, robotics or SCADA"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Progress toward automation architecture, controls leadership and industrial digitalisation"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Combine PLCs with IIoT, edge computing, robotics, AI, digital twins and smart manufacturing"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career-route check"},{"type":"note","label":"Mechatronics Engineering → PLC Programmer","text":"Direct alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"Mechatronics provides a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanical systems"},{"text":"Electrical and electronic systems"},{"text":"Sensors and actuators"},{"text":"Control systems"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Automation"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Industrial systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should additionally develop practical expertise in Ladder Logic, Structured Text, PLC hardware, HMI, SCADA, VFDs, industrial communication, safety systems and commissioning."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Long-range horizons are planning guidance; exact industry requirements should be verified."}]},{"heading":"What to bui